<section class="section">
  <p class="eyebrow">DIRECT DATA VS A HOSTED PROFILE</p>
  <h2>
    Know what
    <br />
    <em>you’re tapping into.</em>
  </h2>
  <div class="comparison">
    <article>
      <h3>Cardistry direct-data</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Contact information lives on the chip.</li>
        <li>Compatible readers can access it offline.</li>
        <li>No monthly Cardistry subscription.</li>
        <li>Updates mean rewriting a writable chip.</li>
        <li>Phone and record-format support must be checked.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>A hosted-profile approach</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>The card typically stores a web address.</li>
        <li>The profile normally needs internet to load.</li>
        <li>Fees vary by provider and plan.</li>
        <li>Online profile details can often be updated remotely.</li>
        <li>Supported URL records can offer broader native NFC behaviour.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="fine">
    A comparison of approaches, not a claim that every competing product has the same
    features or fees.
  </p>
  <a class="inline-link" href="/faq/">
    Check compatibility before you order ↗
  </a>
</section>
